@baseUrl = http://localhost:5273
@seededFoxPostId = 10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

### 1. Create the red fox post used by the end-to-end test
# @name createFoxPost
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Behavior and Habitat of Red Foxes",
  "content": "Red foxes are adaptable mammals. They live in forests, grasslands, and urban areas, and are known for their reddish fur and bushy tails."
}

###
@foxPostId = {{createFoxPost.response.body.$.id}}

### 2. Analyze a sample image and rank it against posts
# In Development demo mode, the analyzer deterministically returns a wolf.
# The Base64 value is a tiny valid PNG placeholder. Demo mode does not use its pixels.
# @name processWolfImage
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/images/process
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://images.example.test/sample-wolf.png",
  "mimeType": "image/png",
  "imageBase64": "iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAIAAACQd1PeAAAADUlEQVQImWNgYGD4DwABBAEAHnOcQAAAAABJRU5ErkJggg=="
}

###
@wolfImageId = {{processWolfImage.response.body.$.imageId}}

### 3. Confirm the wolf image was rejected for the red fox post
# Expected rejectionReason: "Animal category mismatch: expected fox, detected wolf"
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{foxPostId}}/images
Accept: application/json

### 4. A manual approval of the guarded mismatch should return 409 Conflict
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/reviews
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "postId": "{{foxPostId}}",
  "imageId": "{{wolfImageId}}",
  "isApproved": true
}

### 5. Manually reject the recommendation and save a reviewer explanation
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/reviews
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "postId": "{{foxPostId}}",
  "imageId": "{{wolfImageId}}",
  "isApproved": false,
  "rejectionReason": "Animal category mismatch: expected fox, detected wolf"
}

### 6. Confirm demo seed data is available immediately after startup
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{seededFoxPostId}}/images
Accept: application/json

### 7. Example missing post response
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/images
Accept: application/json
